   "etymology": "From Proto-Albanian *mar(en)-, from Proto-Indo-European *merh₂- (“to pack (up)”) or Proto-Indo-European *(s)mer- (“to assign, allot”), cognate with Ancient Greek μείρομαι (meíromai, “receive as one's portion”), Latin mereō, merx and Hittite 𒈥𒀝 (mark, “to divide a sacrifice”). Alternatively derived from Proto-Albanian *marna, a deverbative from Proto-Indo-European *méh₂-r̥ (“hand”), and compared with Ancient Greek μᾰ́ρη (mắrē, “hand”), Latin manus (“hand”).",
